# Every setting Droid Office reads from the environment.
#
# The office does not load .env files. Export a setting in the shell that starts the office
# (`export DROID_OFFICE_CITY="Berlin"`), or set it in its systemd unit as an `Environment=` line
# (`Environment=DROID_OFFICE_CITY=Berlin`) or in the unit's `EnvironmentFile=` (an office deployed
# with deploy/aws.sh reads /etc/droid-office/env).
#
# Every line below is commented out, so nothing changes until you uncomment it. Unset is the
# default; an empty value is not always the same as unset. A command-line flag wins over its
# environment variable.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The office (droid-office)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the office keeps its data when started without a [dir] (--home). Default: ~/droid-office.
# DROID_OFFICE_HOME=~/droid-office

# The workspace folder: where the office looks for your existing git checkouts to add as floors
# (--projects). Nothing is cloned. Default: a code folder in the home folder (~/Workspace, ~/code,
# ~/repos…), else the home folder, or the Workspace folder picked in Settings.
# DROID_OFFICE_PROJECTS=~/Workspace

# Where the Chromium the Whiteboard renders cards with is downloaded and launched from. The office
# and the Mac app use this one folder, and the office hands it to
# Playwright as PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH. Default: the droid-office/browsers folder in your cache
# folder (~/Library/Caches on macOS, $XDG_CACHE_HOME or ~/.cache on Linux, %LOCALAPPDATA% on Windows).
# DROID_OFFICE_BROWSERS_PATH=~/.cache/droid-office/browsers

# Port to listen on (--port). Default: 4600.
# PORT=4600

# The Droid command that new workers run (--agent). Default: droid.
# DROID_OFFICE_AGENT=droid

# Optional: the example custom worker-label adapter (bin/worker-label-openrouter.mjs).
# A Mac app opened from Finder may not inherit shell exports; use its --key-file argument instead.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your-openrouter-key

# Extra arguments for Droid, split like a shell would (--agent-args). Default: none.
# DROID_OFFICE_AGENT_ARGS="--auto medium"

# The most workers the office runs at once, across every floor: a whole number from 1 to 500
# (--max-workers). It can be lowered from Settings but not raised past this. Default: no limit.
# DROID_OFFICE_MAX_WORKERS=6

# A real city, or "lat,lon", whose live forecast from open-meteo.com drives the weather
# (--city). Default: none; the weather is made up.
# DROID_OFFICE_CITY="Portland, Oregon"

# Pin the weather: clear, cloudy, rain, storm, snow or fog (--weather). Default: not pinned.
# DROID_OFFICE_WEATHER=clear

# Any non-empty value skips the first-start walkthrough (which folder your projects are in, the first
# project), and `droid-office setup` asks nothing, even in a terminal. Default: unset.
# CI=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Mac app (src/desktop)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1 skips the Mac app's "Apple M-series Pro chip or better" startup check. It exists for CI only:
# GitHub's macOS runners are base-chip virtual machines, so the packaged app's startup check could
# not run there otherwise. The macOS 14 and Apple silicon checks still apply. Do not set it on a
# Mac you use: the app is built, tuned and tested for Pro, Max and Ultra chips only. Default: unset.
# DROID_OFFICE_ALLOW_ANY_CHIP=1

# Diagnostic only: a file the Mac app appends one line to for every input step (what the native view
# saw, and what went to the page), to find out why a key or click does nothing. It contains the
# text typed, so use it for a hand test only. Default: unset (nothing is written).
# DROID_OFFICE_INPUT_TRACE=/tmp/droid-office-input-trace.log

# Diagnostic only: how the Mac app's native presenter puts frames on the display. `direct` (the default)
# shows each frame at the next refresh; `paced` holds each frame to the display's refresh grid at the 40 and
# 60 FPS limits so the cadence is exact, but measured about 15 to 20 ms later in a window; `link` draws on
# CAMetalDisplayLink updates, which is exact but shows every frame about five refreshes (40 ms at 120 Hz)
# later in a window. `office.presenterStats()` reports the mode in use. There is no setting for it; leave it unset.
# DROID_OFFICE_PRESENT_MODE=paced

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Developer checkouts deployed with deploy/aws.sh (deploy/provision.sh sets these for you)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1 lets the office upgrade itself from its UI: it builds the new version, then exits, so only set
# it under a supervisor that restarts it (systemd Restart=always), on a git checkout that is on a
# branch. Default: off.
# DROID_OFFICE_SELF_UPDATE=1
